  "verbalization": "Azadiradionolide appears to have multiple targets that ultimately converge on SNB-78, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The first pathway links Azadiradionolide to SNU-387, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, a compound that in turn targets SNB-78. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Azadiradionolide influences SNU-387, which then affects SNB-78. In another pathway, Azadiradionolide directly targets Fucosyltransferase 6, which is targeted by Lumiliximab, also leading to SNB-78. A third pathway shows Azadiradionolide targeting SNU-387, which is also targeted by Arundinol B, which in turn targets SNB-78. These findings suggest that Azadiradionolide may act through multiple distinct pathways, each leading to SNB-78, thereby supporting a broader role in modulating cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Azadiradionolide to influence SNB-78 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or receptor modulation.",
